"Outside the Sultan's Palace"
"To the east rises a marvelously constructed palace of domes and towers, the

home of the Sultan of Narak.  North and south runs Palace Street, and to the

west the shops of Main Street can be seen, with scores of merchants going from

store to store to trade, or to gather the local gossip.  A large brass gong

adorns the palace wall to the east next to an ornately-crafted gate.

