#36060
"The Palace of the Sultan"
"The sand-colored streets of Narak give way to the white marble of the interior

of the sultan's palace.  A spiraling stair leads upward to the throne room,

and to the north, you see an oakenwood door leading toward the sultan's

private chambers.  The palace gates to the west are much too massive to be

pushed open, but a large crank mounted in the wall beside it might have

something to do with its operation.  A strange statue of a quite rotund gnome

stands in the southwest corner next to a potted plant.

"
